# Flywheel framework (managed block — edits outside the markers are yours, inside are flywheel's)

Project: (one line — what this project is; seed prompt fills this)

Read `flywheel/INDEX.md` now; it indexes everything (session protocol, on-demand docs).

## Session protocol
1. Read `flywheel/STATUS.md` first — resume from it, don't re-derive. Then
   `bash flywheel/check.sh`: drift warnings = work done outside the framework —
   triage, backfill ledgers/docs, note in STATUS.md.
2. Route work per `flywheel/ORCHESTRATION.md` §1. The six tiers are opencode subagents
   (defined in opencode.json under "agent"); delegate with the templates in
   `flywheel/TEMPLATES.md`.
3. Before ending / context low: wrapup — update STATUS.md + `flywheel/state/*.json`,
   `bash flywheel/check.sh`, rebuild dashboard (`python3 flywheel/dashboard/build.py`),
   commit per `flywheel/GIT.md`.

## Hard rules (point-of-use duplicates — keep identical to INDEX.md)
- HR1. Never Read a file listed in `flywheel/FACTS.md` §Big files (or any file > 200 KB)
  wholesale — slice via grep/jq/python, or delegate to `utility`.
- HR2. Model names / effort values / API params come from `flywheel/config.json` +
  `flywheel/FACTS.md` only. Missing → write `Pending verification`, never invent.
- HR3. No agent declares its own work complete — dispatch `verifier` / `auditor`.
- HR4. Ask-vs-act is governed by `flywheel/AUTONOMY.md`; its level-invariant rows bind
  at every autonomy level.

Note: agent model strings in opencode.json ("provider/model-id") must mirror
`flywheel/config.json` tiers.<tier>.adapters.opencode — the seed prompt fills both from live
provider docs.
<!-- flywheel:end -->
